import ClayStatement.Fefferman
import ClayStatement.Bridge
import ClayStatement.BridgeConverse

/-!
# ClayStatement: Fefferman's literal statements and the bridge to the authors' options

Root module of the `ClayStatement` library (a default build target). It imports the literal statements (`Fefferman`), the
bridge in the direction the solve needs together with the A and B correspondences (`Bridge`), and the converse directions
for C and D (`BridgeConverse`), so a default build checks all four alternatives in both directions.
-/
